Atlas overlay patch 0053: ui/firstrun-page
Why: a new profile opens the Atlas first-run page (four screens, WolOS look) instead of the
upstream setup bundle. The inherited series already shows the setup host while the profile has not
completed it and keeps the engine's own first run away, so the startup check and the host stay as
they are (smallest hunk). Only what the host serves changes: the controller serves the page of
components/atlas_pages/setup/ through the shared page source of patch 0010, and the bundle's
entries leave the resource ids, the pak list, the browser deps and the root resource file (the
bundle's deps.ini section stays: the inherited i18n tools read its version; nothing builds or ships
the unpacked bundle). A first-run preference or a policy cannot
replace the page; a new component is what the page is.
Files: chrome/browser/ui/webui/onboarding/onboarding_page_ui.cc, chrome/browser/ui/webui/BUILD.gn, chrome/browser/BUILD.gn, chrome/chrome_paks.gni, tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec, chrome/app/generated_resources.grd, chrome/app/generated_resources.grd.gritdeps
Test filter: *AtlasFirstRun*; reel-check scene R04 (a fresh profile opens the setup page once; zero requests off the page)
Rebase risk: M (removes lines the inherited onboarding patch adds; if it changes them, only this patch needs the same edit)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited, platform and 0010 patches applied

